XLeRobot ROS integration

Robot source and mesh geometry derive from Vector-Wangel/XLeRobot, maintained
by Victor Wang and contributors, pinned in the upstream Git submodule at
b017b5e6354bd9f61f4247a920c72622ca0aade0. Upstream's Apache-2.0 license remains
with its files. The ROS URDF preserves upstream geometry and kinematic facts
with separately documented simulated camera and IMU mounts.

Docker and operator-script organization follows the local mr_handy and
grove-g1 projects. Nav2 parameters adapt ROS 2 Jazzy nav2_bringup defaults
(Open Navigation and contributors). RTAB-Map integration follows the
introlab/rtabmap_ros RGB-D and IMU examples (Mathieu Labbe and contributors).

Ekumen's LeKiwi omni-base modeling article by Franco Cipollone is credited
as a design reference. This stack adapts its roller contact topology from
Aditya Kamath's pinned lekiwi_mujoco implementation. The adapted runtime model
uses a floating chassis, three driven wheel joints and 48 passive rollers;
XLeRobot's original planar chassis actuators are removed. Added contact geometry
and the 8 kg cart mass are documented simulation assumptions. Four passive
cart casters and their vertical compliance model support the cart. Caster
visuals are split from the original ManiSkill meshes; mounting connectors
derive from upstream hardware/XLeRobot 0-3-0 new wheel connector.stl.
Cart alignment and connector height fits are recorded in cart_mount.yaml.

Complete cart, arm-mount, head and wrist-camera visuals are restored from
the pinned upstream simulation/Maniskill/assets/xlerobot URDF and meshes.
The furnished home layout and preparation helpers are adapted from mr_handy.
RoboCasa-compatible Lightwheel assets are attributed to NVIDIA / Lightwheel,
licensed CC-BY-4.0; selected source/prepared files, license and pinned provenance
are retained under assets/robocasa.

Robocore Viz browser dashboard and bridge are vendored from the Mr Handy
package, originally based on Dheera Venkatraman's ROSboard and Robocore's
base101 fork. Its BSD license, third-party notices and extraction provenance
are retained in src/robocore_viz/LICENSE and PROVENANCE.md.

LeKiwi ROS 2 and sts_hardware_interface by Aditya Kamath (Kamath Robotics)
are retained as pinned Git submodules under dependencies/lekiwi_ros2. Their
Apache-2.0 licenses and attribution remain in the respective repositories.
The XLeRobot wrapper uses their control defaults, command switch, kinematics,
passive omniwheel roller topology and installed STS hardware driver; XLeRobot-specific adapters live in src/.

The optional Mod101 arm configuration uses Robocore Labs' mod101 repository,
pinned at e0b450111f3fad7a514446c07a642c384dd5c332 under dependencies/mod101.
The reusable arm macro supplies meshes, rail geometry, inertias and joint limits.
Its PG gripper adapts NormaCore's Parallel Jaw Gripper; the original Apache-2.0
license, source STEP and attribution remain in mod101_tool_pggripper.
Arm attachment poses and MuJoCo servo/contact settings are local simulation
assumptions, not a validated hardware mounting or motor calibration.
